.TH SDL_Mutex 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_Mutex \- A means to serialize access to a resource between threads.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mutex.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_Mutex SDL_Mutex;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mutexes (short for \(dqmutual exclusion\(dq) are a synchronization primitive that allows exactly one thread to proceed at a time\[char46]
.PP
Wikipedia has a thorough explanation of the concept:
.PP
https://en\[char46]wikipedia\[char46]org/wiki/Mutex

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

